  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By De Morgan&#39;s theorem, we have</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/44f234dd-ae1c-4509-a128-71c22405ecd0-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 126px;\" /></p><p>Here the output of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. This output is fed as inputs to NAND gate and the output is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>, when when again fed as input to NAND gate to get output as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>.</p>",
